**Hello World with Chakra UI in TypeScript**

To create a "Hello World" application with Chakra UI in TypeScript, you'll need to install the required packages and set up a basic project structure. Here's a step-by-step guide:

### Step 1: Create a new project

Create a new project using the following command:

```bash
npx create-react-app my-app --template typescript
```

This will create a new React project with TypeScript support.

### Step 2: Install Chakra UI

Install Chakra UI using npm:

```bash
npm install @chakra-ui/react @emotion/react @emotion/styled framer-motion
```

### Step 3: Create a new component

Create a new file called `HelloWorld.tsx` in the `src` directory:

```typescript
// src/HelloWorld.tsx
import React from 'react';
import { Box, Text } from '@chakra-ui/react';

const HelloWorld: React.FC = () => {
  return (
    <Box
      display="flex"
      justifyContent="center"
      alignItems="center"
      height="100vh"
      bg="gray.100"
    >
      <Text fontSize="4xl" fontWeight="bold" color="blue.500">
        Hello World!
      </Text>
    </Box>
  );
};

export default HelloWorld;
```

### Step 4: Update the App component

Update the `App.tsx` file to render the `HelloWorld` component:

```typescript
// src/App.tsx
import React from 'react';
import HelloWorld from './HelloWorld';

function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      <HelloWorld />
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```

